<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#earl-of-derby">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Earl of Derby</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derby">Derby</a> is a title in the peerage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> held since 1485 by the Stanley family. Thomas Stanley received it from Henry VII after the Battle of Bosworth, and his heirs were also Lords of Mann until 1736. The 7th Earl, James Stanley, held the island for Charles I and was executed in 1651, and later earls included the Victorian prime minister Edward Smith-Stanley, 14th Earl.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/earl-of-derby.jpg" alt="Earl of Derby" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Stanley,_Earls_of_Derby.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
